zig-engine TP=3/4 direct RoCE: with a fixed GID index, probe every rail's subnet beyond two ranks so the routes can pair
rails, but only when the probed RoCE v2 IPv4 GID is the fixed index's own (railAddr); a mismatched rail is left out of
the routes instead of being described by another GID's address, and if a required pair of ranks is left without a
shared subnet there is no complete route plan, so every rank keeps NCCL. Host tests: railAddr, and its effect on a
triangle's routes.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0010-zig-glm-tpn-roce-probe.patch

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm_cuda/cuda_comm.zig b/zig/src/families/glm_cuda/cuda_comm.zig
